How the build enforces this file:

  The "basic template" below is the canonical header that the build checks and inserts
  (Spotless, configured in pom.xml) immediately before the `package` declaration of every
  Java file changed relative to origin/master. The block is enforced exactly as written,
  with `$YEAR` in place of the example year range below: the build keeps the end of the
  `Copyright <first>-<last>` range current and never changes the first year.

  The contributor template below is deliberately excluded from header enforcement: a file
  carrying extra `Copyright <year> <name>` lines is left byte-for-byte unchanged in its
  header (stale year ranges included), while its body is still formatted. The same applies
  to any other header shape that is neither the basic template nor the compact variant
  (`Copyright $YEAR Julien Ponge, René Krell and the IzPack team.`) also configured in
  pom.xml.

